 # tokenization examples
 tok_audit=read_json(out/'input_tokenization_audit.json');example=tok_audit['records'][0]['resource_numbers']
 h=['# Hardware input and embedding audit','','## Prompt route','','The canonical schema supplies learned device tokens, selected-clock tokens and the `<CLOCK>` response prefix, objective token, per-device numerical capacities/available-resource counts/percentages, source/action markers, then the autoregressive directive prefix. All 18 grid requests use the same supported clock menu `[3.33, 5, 10]` and vary the selected specified clock. The resource budget changes the numeric available counts and percentages. Full prompt strings and token IDs are frozen under `prompts/`; the 20% request is a separate historical row.','','For example, the V4 prompt tokenizes `BRAM_18K`, `DSP`, `FF`, and `LUT` numeric counts as ordinary tokenizer pieces; the values are not dedicated learned hardware special tokens. `input_tokenization_audit.json` records the exact token IDs/spans for every numeric count and percentage. The device and clock markers are dedicated added tokens, and the fixed selected-clock response prefix is already part of the canonical inference path.','','## Special-token rows','','The V4 checkpoint has 140 trainable special-token input rows. PEFT’s `trainable_tokens_original` stores the exact resized-base initialization; `trainable_tokens_delta` in this PEFT version is the full learned row, not an additive delta tensor. The report therefore compares final rows with their preserved initialization. All 140 have trainable parameters, though many had zero observed update. These rows were added to the tokenizer after the pretrained vocabulary was loaded, so “initial” means resize-time initialization, not an original pretrained semantic vector.','','| Token | Initial→trained cosine | Relative row update L2 | Interpretation |','|---|---:|---:|---|']
 for name,x in hardware_updates.items():h.append(f"| `{name}` | {x['initial_to_trained_cosine']:.4f} | {x['relative_update_l2']:.3f} | learned input row; geometric relation is not physical device similarity |")
 h+=['','The ZCU104 device token has cosine `'+fmt(hardware_updates['<DEV=XCZU7EV_FFVC1156_2E>']['initial_to_trained_cosine'])+'` to its resize-time row; XCU200 is `'+fmt(hardware_updates['<DEV=XCU200_FSGD2104_2E>']['initial_to_trained_cosine'])+'`. The 10 ns and 5 ns clock rows move substantially, while the 3.33 ns row changes little in this adapter. Those are observations about learned token weights only. The learned row vectors and pairwise cosine matrices are saved in `special_token_embeddings.npz` and `hardware_token_cosines.json`.','','## Does target information reach choices?','','Yes, as an observed representational effect: every matched device/clock/budget contrast changes the selected decision vectors, with median relative movement reported in `STAGE1_32_LAYER_ANALYSIS.md`. In the controlled score comparisons all legal RHS candidates remain identical. Several candidate margins change even where the winner remains stable. The 10 ns/100% device pair had zero assignment changes; the budget contrast produced two L5 winner changes in XCU200/50%. No result demonstrates a QoR improvement or that budget feasibility was binding.','','The all-layer activation patch places the controlled R1 post-attention vector into a receiver at the corresponding directive-token position. Four sampled pairs changed sign, with exactly unchanged same-state placebo margins. This supports decision relevance of selected late/intermediate activations, while leaving mediation across all layers and physical optimization unproven.']
 (PACKAGE/'HARDWARE_ENCODING_AUDIT.md').write_text('\n'.join(h)+'\n')
 # structure report
 st=['# GEMV compiler structure × target analysis','','## RC3 authority and verified structural contrast','','The original input bytes and action metadata match the read-only GNN branch’s frozen RC3 source manifest. That canonical graph records 66 nodes, 106 edges, and five matched actions; the original MLIR and graph are copied byte-for-byte into `inputs/` with the upstream manifest and checksums. The GNN authority is commit `172e05a69650a666c323955ea78cb501fd9364c2`.','','The original source provides `A[32][32]`, `x[32]`, `y[32]`, accesses `A[i][j]` and `x[j]`, and nested 32-iteration loops. RC3 exposes affine indices, loop nesting, action-to-operation/memory relationships, and the scalarized compiler representation of `y`. Its L5 inner loop contains `%arg2` as `iter_args`, multiplication, addition and `affine.yield`; this is compiler evidence for a scalar carried recurrence, not a memory-independence statement.','','The new valid diagnostic program uses initialized function inputs copied into local arrays and makes every partial/final result observable. `reduce32` is a scalar reduction. `independent32` writes each product independently and sets `y[i]=0`; it intentionally changes the algorithm and outputs. `reduce32_rename` consistently renames variables and retains the same recurrence. Each compiled with the authenticated `cgeist`/MLIR V2.2 RC3 pipeline and retained L1–L5. Deterministic numerical checks reported maximum absolute errors of 1.22e-4 for the reduction and rename control and 0 for the independent-product oracle; the reduction/rename check is within its float32 tolerance.','','| Program | Source SHA-256 | Graph SHA-256 | RC3 scalar recurrence | Meaning relation |','|---|---|---|---|---|']
 for x in srcs:st.append(f"| {x['name']} | `{x['source_sha256']}` | `{x['graph_sha256']}` | {'yes' if x['kind']=='reduction' else 'no explicit scalar carried result'} | {'rename control' if x['syntax_control_of'] else ('different per-iteration program' if x['kind']=='independent' else 'initialized reduction')} |")
 st += ['', '## Target and structure interaction','','All three diagnostic sources were scored under eight matched contexts spanning both devices, 10/3.33 ns, and 100/25% requested budgets. Requests, prompts, source hashes, graph hashes, full legal candidate scores, and all 32-layer states are retained. Controlled comparisons use the original R1 assignment as the common preceding directive context. The official natural decoder outputs are separate and were not replaced by counterfactual argmaxes.','','Across controlled positions, the independent-vs-reduction median relative vector movement was '+fmt(float(np.median([x['independent_vs_reduce'] for x in structures if x['prefix_mode']=='controlled'])))+'; rename-vs-reduction movement was '+fmt(float(np.median([x['rename_vs_reduce'] for x in structures if x['prefix_mode']=='controlled'])))+'. At L5 unroll these medians were '+fmt(float(np.median([x['independent_vs_reduce'] for x in structures if x['prefix_mode']=='controlled' and x['field']=='auto{_UNROLL_L5}'])))+' and '+fmt(float(np.median([x['rename_vs_reduce'] for x in structures if x['prefix_mode']=='controlled' and x['field']=='auto{_UNROLL_L5}'])))+', respectively. A source edit that changes computation therefore moves the states, but the meaning-preserving rename also moves them strongly. This is not recurrence-decoding evidence.','','At ZCU104/10 ns/100% under the R1 controlled prefix, the L5 unroll scores rank `4` above `2` for reduction (margin '+fmt(float(next(x['margin'] for x in results['reduce32__SUB_ZCU104_10P0NS_100PCT']['trace_records'] if x['prefix_mode']=='controlled' and x['field']=='auto{_UNROLL_L5}')))+'), and rank `2` above `4` for independent iterations (margin '+fmt(float(next(x['margin'] for x in results['independent32__SUB_ZCU104_10P0NS_100PCT']['trace_records'] if x['prefix_mode']=='controlled' and x['field']=='auto{_UNROLL_L5}')))+'). The actual natural top directive is the same (`UNROLL_L5=0`) for both. The rename control retains `UNROLL_L5=4` as the controlled argmax but flips `PIPE_L5` to a near-tie preference for 0; reduction prefers 1. L1 dimension ranks 1 for reduction and independent, but the rename source picks dimension 2. These observations motivate a syntax-robust compiler-memory ablation; they do not establish an optimal partition or loop pragma.','','## Action-specific interpretation','','- **L1 A:** C exposes array dimensions and `A[i][j]`; RC3 binds the memory operations and ordered indices to L4/L5. Across the original hardware grid L1 stays block/2/dim1. The rename diagnostic changes the L1 dimension preference despite preserving the recurrence program. Correct access-direction reasoning is not established.\n- **L2 x:** C exposes `x[j]`; RC3 binds it to the inner-loop induction. Factor is stable on the original direct one-factor target contrasts, changing only in a combined tight-clock/tight-budget cell; no port or QoR inference follows.\n- **L3 y:** Source says `y[32]` and returns `y[0]`; RC3 records scalarized compiler storage. L3 changes under combined constraints and lexical rename; no output-resource benefit is measured.\n- **L4 outer:** RC3 verifies trip count 32, depth 0 and child loop L5. The original grid retains PIPE0/UNROLL2. Source contrasts change some conditional scores but not the selected value; useful structural use is unresolved.\n- **L5 inner:** RC3 verifies the scalar SSA recurrence in the reduction source. Candidate preferences depend on the source variant under a fixed prefix, but the natural directive remains the same for reduction and independent. The controlled difference is confounded by different computation/output and token sequence; a syntax-only rename can also move preferences.','','The structure×target score difference-in-differences for the fixed candidate pairs is small (median absolute margin interaction by target factor: device '+fmt(float(np.median([abs(x['score_margin_interaction']) for x in ints if x.get('kind')=='device' and 'score_margin_interaction' in x])))+', clock '+fmt(float(np.median([abs(x['score_margin_interaction']) for x in ints if x.get('kind')=='clock' and 'score_margin_interaction' in x])))+', budget '+fmt(float(np.median([abs(x['score_margin_interaction']) for x in ints if x.get('kind')=='budget' and 'score_margin_interaction' in x])))+'). This supports only weak, small-sample structure×target score interactions under the tested alternatives. The model outputs no “correct” target-optimal label because QoR was not measured.']
 (PACKAGE/'GEMV_STRUCTURE_TARGET_ANALYSIS.md').write_text('\n'.join(st)+'\n')
